  "reviews": [
    {
      "game": "Alien: Isolation",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/305/450x258/alien-isolation-pc-mac-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1787079600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/305-buy-alien-isolation-pc-mac-game-steam/",
      "user": "O_rélie_69",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/31234274-1778239497.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "un jeu solo avec une histoire prenante, captivante, très stratégique pour s'en sortir, il ne faut pas simplement se cacher, car l'IA des aliens des humains et des androïdes évolue à chaque fois. ce qui rajoute du stress .\n\n\n\n2 petits bémol le fait de regarder la carte casse l'immersion dans le jeu , et les mini codes pour débloquer certaines portes deviennent pénibles à la longue. Mais les graphismes , les effets sonores et les musiques angoissantes rattrapent ca, les aliens sont bien terrifiants. hâte de jouer au 2"
    },
    {
      "game": "Stranded Deep",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/18281/450x258/stranded-deep-pc-mac-steam-cover.jpg?v=1787079600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/18281-buy-stranded-deep-pc-mac-steam/",
      "user": "Skyler Colt",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/19847532-1786172778.jpg",
      "sentiment": "dislike",
      "content": "⭐☆☆☆☆\n\n\n\nStranded Deep feels like it is actively trying to punish new players.\n\n\n\nThere is basically no proper tutorial, so you're thrown onto an island with no idea what you're supposed to do. You get poisoned five minutes into the game, but the antidote requires a crafting level you obviously don't have yet. Good luck figuring that out.\n\n\n\nThe crafting system is unnecessarily confusing, resources are limited at the beginning, and the game explains almost nothing. We spent half our time Googling how to do basic things that should have been explained in the game.\n\n\n\nThen there's the multiplayer. If both players die, instead of simply respawning or reloading the save, you're thrown back into the lobby. Then, every single time you try to join again, you have to sit there for five minutes waiting for the world to sync.\n\n\n\nAnd don't even get me started on trying to interact with objects. You find useful raft parts underwater, but the game barely tells you how to move or use them.\n\n\n\nThe survival concept is genuinely fun, and exploring islands and shipwrecks can be exciting, but the terrible lack of explanation, confusing mechanics, clunky controls, and painfully slow co-op syncing make the experience incredibly frustrating.\n\n\n\nThis game doesn't feel challenging because survival is difficult. It feels challenging because you're constantly fighting the game's terrible design.\n\n\n\nWould I recommend it? Absolutely not unless you have unlimited patience."
    },
    {
      "game": "The Lord of the Rings: Return to Moria",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/14332/450x258/the-lord-of-the-rings-return-to-moria-pc-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1787079600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/14332-buy-the-lord-of-the-rings-return-to-moria-pc-game-steam/",
      "user": "gamer-16cf67a",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Good, had fun.\n\n\n\ntook some time to become fun, because you need to mine resources a lot at the start, but after some time it becomes easier, and the focus is more on exploration.\n\n\n\nThere is a lot of repetition, however."
    },
    {
      "game": "WitchSpring R",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/15138/450x258/witchspring-r-pc-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1787079600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/15138-buy-witchspring-r-pc-game-steam/",
      "user": "Clayn",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "One of the most underrated gems of game in general and especially in the jrpg market. \n\nThe story is written so well, far off the usual cliché stuffed \"friendship against evil\" themes of most of those rpgs. The story starts off silly and cutesy and evolves from every chapter constantly to a mature story with heavy themes and still keeps it lighthearted where it needs to be.\n\n\n\nA fun turn based Rpg with cool creature collecting and a light spell crafting mechanic to tinker around a little for customization.\n\n\n\nI would love to play all the other titles, but they are all mobile exclusive and dont exist anymore. Are you fricking kidding me?"
    }
